  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The final greeting and response followed by the Requiem dismissal and Amen, as prescribed by the 1962 Roman Missal. These are selected from the complete Ordo and its explicit replacement rule, not presented as one uninterrupted printed Requiem block. The low-Mass dismissal is said by the celebrant facing the altar; its generic sung-Mass actor is left unassigned because the two Mass-form choices do not distinguish a Missa cantata from a solemn Mass. Ritus XI.3 assigns the cantata chant to the celebrant. Placeat remains a separate following prayer; the final blessing is omitted. The Last Gospel is normally retained, except when the separately prescribed absolution over the tumulus follows (RG 507 c, 508–510; Ritus XI.1, XI.3, XII.4, XIII.1).",
    "source": {
      "method": "Separately read against the Benziger Editio iuxta typicam and the distinct Vatican setting of the 1962 Roman Missal; the printed clauses and replacement rubrics determine this complete recension. The witness headers and apparatus distinguish source transcription from the rule-derived reading.",
